---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Custom Frappe Applications | Ecosoft"
  description="Ecosoft builds custom business applications on the Frappe framework — the same platform powering ERPNext — for bespoke requirements beyond standard ERP modules."
>


  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Frappe Apps</p>
      <h1>Custom business applications — built on the same platform as your ERP.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        The Frappe framework powers ERPNext — but it also powers any custom application you need to build.
        When your requirement goes beyond what standard ERP modules can handle, Ecosoft builds bespoke Frappe applications
        that integrate natively with your existing system, share the same database, and work within the same interface.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Discuss Your Custom App Requirement</a>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="btn btn-outline">See a Frappe App Demo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT IS FRAPPE -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="cta-strip-grid" style="align-items:start;">
        <div>
          <h2>What is the Frappe framework?</h2>
          <p>
            Frappe is a full-stack Python web framework with a built-in ORM, role-based access control,
            REST API layer, background job processing, and a React-based frontend component library.
            It's designed specifically for building complex business applications — and ERPNext is its flagship implementation.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
            Building on Frappe means your custom application shares the same architecture, authentication,
            and database as your ERPNext installation. No integration layer. No data duplication. No separate login.
          </p>
          <ul style="margin-top:1.5rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0.5rem; list-style:none; padding:0;">
            <li>✓ Python backend, modern JavaScript frontend</li>
            <li>✓ Built-in role-based permissions</li>
            <li>✓ REST API out of the box</li>
            <li>✓ Background jobs, email, and notification handling</li>
            <li>✓ Printable document formats with custom templates</li>
            <li>✓ Webhooks and third-party integrations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="info-card" style="padding:2rem;">
            <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Frappe in numbers</h3>
            <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1.5rem; margin-top:1rem;">
              <div style="text-align:center;">
                <div style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent);">14+</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Years in production</div>
              </div>
              <div style="text-align:center;">
                <div style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent);">15k+</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-muted);">GitHub stars</div>
              </div>
              <div style="text-align:center;">
                <div style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent);">100+</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Community apps</div>
              </div>
              <div style="text-align:center;">
                <div style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent);">MIT</div>
                <div style="font-size:0.875rem; color:var(--text-muted);">Open licence</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT WE BUILD -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="text-align:center;">What Ecosoft builds on Frappe</h2>
      <p class="section-lead" style="text-align:center;">Examples of custom applications we've delivered for clients who needed more than standard ERP modules.</p>
      <div class="cards-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap:1.5rem; margin-top:2.5rem;">

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">🛰️</div>
          <h4>Satellite BOM management</h4>
          <p>For EOS Orbit — multi-level BOM management for aerospace components with serial number tracking, integration test workflows, and ISO 9001 traceability built as a native Frappe app.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">📐</div>
          <h4>Specification-to-BOM automation</h4>
          <p>For Square Panel Systems — a custom module that generates production BOMs directly from sales order specifications, eliminating manual BOM creation for every custom-configuration order.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">🏛️</div>
          <h4>Government budget encumbrance</h4>
          <p>For NSTDA and NXPO — budget control modules that enforce hard encumbrance limits, track multi-fund allocations, and produce government-standard budget execution reports.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">📊</div>
          <h4>Custom reporting portals</h4>
          <p>Management portals that surface ERP data in role-specific views — board dashboards, production floor displays, customer-facing order trackers — all built on Frappe.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">🔗</div>
          <h4>Third-party integration bridges</h4>
          <p>Frappe apps that connect ERPNext to external systems — e-commerce platforms, payment gateways, logistics APIs, government portals, and legacy line-of-business systems.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-card">
          <div class="info-card-icon">📋</div>
          <h4>Industry-specific workflows</h4>
          <p>Custom document types, approval chains, and process workflows for requirements that standard ERPNext modules don't address — built to OCA-equivalent quality standards.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUR APPROACH -->
  <section class="section" style="background: var(--surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; text-align:center;">
        <h2>Built to last, not just to ship</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Ecosoft is an active contributor to the Frappe/ERPNext ecosystem. Our custom apps are built to the same
          quality standards we apply to upstream contributions — documented, tested, and maintainable across Frappe versions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap:1.5rem; margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <div class="info-card">
          <h4>Version-safe</h4>
          <p>Custom apps that follow Frappe extension patterns survive version upgrades — not apps that patch core files.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h4>Documented</h4>
          <p>Every custom doctype, script, and integration is documented — so your team (or any developer) can maintain it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h4>Open-source by default</h4>
          <p>Custom apps are your property, built in the open. No proprietary lock-in to Ecosoft for ongoing access.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-card">
          <h4>Ecosystem-aware</h4>
          <p>We check the community ecosystem before building custom — often an existing Frappe app does the job, saving months of development.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Have a requirement that standard ERP modules can't handle?</h2>
      <p>Describe it to us — we'll assess whether a custom Frappe app is the right solution and scope what it would take to build.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Discuss Your Custom App</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
